  "exerciseName": "{code, select, JUMPING_JACKS{Jumping jacks} HIGH_KNEES{High knees} BUTT_KICKS{Butt kicks} JUMP_ROPE{Jump rope} ARM_CIRCLES{Arm circles} SHOULDER_DISLOCATES{Shoulder dislocates} BAND_PULL_APART{Band pull-apart} HIP_CIRCLES{Hip circles} LEG_SWINGS_FRONT{Leg swings front-back} LEG_SWINGS_SIDE{Leg swings side-to-side} WRIST_CIRCLES{Wrist circles} FINGER_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Finger flexor stretch} FINGER_EXTENSOR_BAND{Finger extensions with band} SCAPULAR_PULL_UP{Scapular pull-up} DEAD_HANG{Dead hang} INCHWORM{Inchworm} EASY_TRAVERSE{Easy traverse} CAT_COW{Cat-cow} THORACIC_ROTATION{Thoracic rotation} WORLDS_GREATEST_STRETCH{Greatest stretch} DEEP_SQUAT_HOLD{Deep squat hold} HIP_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Hip flexor stretch} PIGEON_STRETCH{Pigeon stretch} HAMSTRING_STRETCH{Hamstring stretch} COUCH_STRETCH{Couch stretch} CHILD_POSE{Child pose} DOWNWARD_DOG{Downward dog} COBRA{Cobra} ANKLE_CIRCLES{Ankle circles} CALF_RAISE{Calf raise} SINGLE_LEG_BALANCE{Single-leg balance} SHORT_FOOT{Short foot} TOWEL_SCRUNCH{Towel scrunch} WRIST_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Wrist flexor stretch} SHOULDER_CARS{Shoulder circles (CARs)} HIP_CARS{Hip circles (CARs)} PUSH_UP{Push-up} INCLINE_PUSH_UP{Incline push-up} DIAMOND_PUSH_UP{Diamond push-up} PIKE_PUSH_UP{Pike push-up} RING_PUSH_UP{Ring push-up} RING_DIP{Ring dip} RING_SUPPORT_HOLD{Ring support hold} TRX_CHEST_PRESS{TRX chest press} TRX_TRICEPS_EXTENSION{TRX triceps extension} DUMBBELL_BENCH_PRESS{Dumbbell bench press} OVERHEAD_PRESS{Overhead press} BENCH_PRESS{Bench press} PULL_UP{Pull-up} CHIN_UP{Chin-up} NEGATIVE_PULL_UP{Negative pull-up} RING_ROW{Ring row} TRX_ROW{TRX row} TRX_Y_RAISE{TRX Y-raise} FACE_PULL_BAND{Band face pull} EXTERNAL_ROTATION_BAND{Band external rotation} DUMBBELL_ROW{Dumbbell row} KETTLEBELL_SWING{Kettlebell swing} DEADLIFT{Deadlift} ROMANIAN_DEADLIFT{Romanian deadlift} BODYWEIGHT_SQUAT{Bodyweight squat} GOBLET_SQUAT{Goblet squat} SPLIT_SQUAT{Split squat} BULGARIAN_SPLIT_SQUAT{Bulgarian split squat} REVERSE_LUNGE{Reverse lunge} LATERAL_LUNGE{Lateral lunge} STEP_UP{Step-up} PISTOL_SQUAT_ASSISTED{Assisted pistol squat} GLUTE_BRIDGE{Glute bridge} SINGLE_LEG_GLUTE_BRIDGE{Single-leg glute bridge} HIP_THRUST{Hip thrust} NORDIC_CURL_ASSISTED{Assisted Nordic curl} BACK_SQUAT{Back squat} SINGLE_LEG_CALF_RAISE{Single-leg calf raise} PLANK{Plank} SIDE_PLANK{Side plank} HOLLOW_HOLD{Hollow hold} SUPERMAN_HOLD{Superman hold} DEAD_BUG{Dead bug} BIRD_DOG{Bird dog} HANGING_KNEE_RAISE{Hanging knee raise} HANGING_LEG_RAISE{Hanging leg raise} L_SIT{L-sit} MOUNTAIN_CLIMBER{Mountain climber} RING_FALLOUT{Ring fallout} TRX_PIKE{TRX pike} HANGBOARD_MAX_HANG{Hangboard max hang} HANGBOARD_REPEATER{Hangboard repeaters} HANGBOARD_MIN_EDGE_HANG{Hangboard minimum edge hang} LOCK_OFF_HOLD{Lock-off hold} TUCK_FRONT_LEVER{Tuck front lever} RICE_BUCKET{Rice bucket} WRIST_CURL{Wrist curl} REVERSE_WRIST_CURL{Reverse wrist curl} BOULDER_PROBLEMS{Boulder problems} ROUTE_CLIMBING{Route climbing} ARC_TRAVERSE{ARC traverse} LIMIT_BOULDERING{Limit bouldering} FOUR_BY_FOUR{4x4 boulders} EASY_RUN{Easy run} TEMPO_RUN{Tempo run} INTERVAL_RUN{Interval run} EASY_RIDE{Easy ride} STATIONARY_BIKE_STEADY{Stationary bike, steady} ROWING_ERG{Rowing machine} BURPEE{Burpee} FOAM_ROLL_QUADS{Foam roll quads} FOAM_ROLL_UPPER_BACK{Foam roll upper back} FOAM_ROLL_CALVES{Foam roll calves} FOREARM_MASSAGE{Forearm massage} BOX_BREATHING{Box breathing} WALKING_COOLDOWN{Walking cooldown} other{{code}}}",
  "@exerciseName": {"description": "Localized exercise catalog name by stable code (C51 EXC-007).", "placeholders": {"code": {"type": "String"}}},
  "exerciseInstructions": "{code, select, JUMPING_JACKS{Stand tall. Jump the feet apart while raising the arms overhead, then jump back together with arms down. Keep a light, steady rhythm.} HIGH_KNEES{Run in place, driving each knee up to hip height. Stay tall and land softly on the balls of the feet.} BUTT_KICKS{Jog in place, kicking the heels up toward the glutes. Keep the knees pointing down and the torso upright.} JUMP_ROPE{Turn the rope from the wrists and hop just high enough to clear it. Land softly on the balls of the feet.} ARM_CIRCLES{Extend the arms out to the sides and draw circles, small to large, forward and then backward.} SHOULDER_DISLOCATES{Hold a band wide in front of the hips with straight arms. Raise it overhead and behind the back, then return the same way.} BAND_PULL_APART{Hold a band at shoulder height with straight arms. Pull the hands apart until the band touches the chest, then return slowly.} HIP_CIRCLES{Stand on one leg or hold support. Draw large circles with the knee of the free leg, both directions.} LEG_SWINGS_FRONT{Hold a wall for balance. Swing one straight leg forward and back with control, gradually increasing the range.} LEG_SWINGS_SIDE{Face a wall with hands on it. Swing one leg across the body and out to the side, keeping the torso still.} WRIST_CIRCLES{Interlace the fingers and roll the wrists in circles both directions, then flex and extend each hand.} FINGER_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Extend one arm, palm up. Gently pull the fingers back with the other hand until a mild stretch in the forearm.} FINGER_EXTENSOR_BAND{Loop a small band around the fingertips. Open the hand against the band and close slowly.} SCAPULAR_PULL_UP{Hang from the bar with straight arms. Without bending the elbows, pull the shoulder blades down and together, then relax.} DEAD_HANG{Hang from the bar with straight arms and active shoulders. Breathe calmly and hold.} INCHWORM{From standing, fold forward and walk the hands out to a plank, then walk the feet back to the hands and stand up.} EASY_TRAVERSE{Climb sideways on easy holds, focusing on quiet feet and relaxed grip. Keep the intensity very light.} CAT_COW{On hands and knees, round the back and tuck the chin, then arch the back and lift the head. Move slowly with the breath.} THORACIC_ROTATION{On hands and knees, place one hand behind the head. Rotate the elbow toward the ceiling, opening the chest, then return.} WORLDS_GREATEST_STRETCH{Step into a deep lunge, place the hands inside the front foot, then rotate the same-side arm to the ceiling. Return and repeat.} DEEP_SQUAT_HOLD{Sit into the deepest squat you can with heels down. Use the elbows to gently press the knees out and breathe.} HIP_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Kneel on one knee, the other foot in front. Tuck the pelvis and shift forward until you feel a stretch at the front of the rear hip.} PIGEON_STRETCH{From hands and knees, bring one shin forward across the body and extend the other leg back. Sink the hips and breathe.} HAMSTRING_STRETCH{Place one heel on a low step with a straight knee. Hinge forward from the hips with a flat back until you feel the stretch.} COUCH_STRETCH{Kneel with one shin against a wall, foot up. Step the other foot forward and squeeze the glute of the rear leg.} CHILD_POSE{Kneel and sit back on the heels, then reach the arms forward and rest the forehead down. Breathe into the back.} DOWNWARD_DOG{From a plank, lift the hips up and back into an inverted V. Press the heels toward the floor and lengthen the spine.} COBRA{Lie face down, hands under the shoulders. Press the chest up while keeping the hips on the floor.} ANKLE_CIRCLES{Lift one foot and draw slow circles with the toes in both directions.} CALF_RAISE{Stand tall and rise onto the balls of the feet, pause, then lower slowly under control.} SINGLE_LEG_BALANCE{Stand on one leg with a soft knee. Keep the arch of the foot lifted and hold still, eyes forward.} SHORT_FOOT{Standing or seated, pull the ball of the foot toward the heel to lift the arch without curling the toes. Hold, then relax.} TOWEL_SCRUNCH{Place a towel under the foot and scrunch it toward you with the toes, then spread the toes to release.} WRIST_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Extend one arm with the palm facing away and fingers up. Gently pull the fingers back and hold.} SHOULDER_CARS{Standing tall, draw the largest slow circle you can with one straight arm without moving the torso.} HIP_CARS{Hold support, lift one knee, open it out to the side, extend back, and return in one slow circle. Keep the torso still.} PUSH_UP{Hands under the shoulders in a plank. Lower the chest to the floor with the elbows about 45 degrees from the body, then press up.} INCLINE_PUSH_UP{Hands on a bench or step, body straight. Lower the chest toward the edge and press back up.} DIAMOND_PUSH_UP{Hands close together under the chest, thumbs and index fingers touching. Lower and press with the elbows close to the body.} PIKE_PUSH_UP{Start in a downward dog with hips high. Bend the elbows to lower the top of the head toward the floor, then press up.} RING_PUSH_UP{Rings low, hands turned slightly out. Lower the chest between the rings and press up while keeping the rings still.} RING_DIP{Support on rings with straight arms. Lower until the shoulders are near the hands, then press up and turn the rings out at the top.} RING_SUPPORT_HOLD{Support the body on the rings with straight arms, rings turned slightly out, shoulders down. Hold still.} TRX_CHEST_PRESS{Face away from the anchor, handles at chest height. Lean forward and lower the chest between the handles, then press back.} TRX_TRICEPS_EXTENSION{Face away from the anchor, arms extended overhead. Bend the elbows to lower the head between the hands, then extend.} DUMBBELL_BENCH_PRESS{Lie on the bench with dumbbells over the chest. Lower to the sides of the chest, then press up until the arms are straight.} OVERHEAD_PRESS{Stand with dumbbells at the shoulders. Press straight overhead until the arms lock, then lower under control.} BENCH_PRESS{Lie on the bench, grip the bar slightly wider than the shoulders. Lower to the mid-chest and press up.} PULL_UP{Hang with an overhand grip. Pull the chest toward the bar until the chin clears it, then lower fully.} CHIN_UP{Hang with an underhand grip, hands shoulder width. Pull up until the chin clears the bar, then lower fully.} NEGATIVE_PULL_UP{Jump or step to the top position with the chin over the bar. Lower yourself as slowly as possible to straight arms.} RING_ROW{Lean back holding the rings with straight arms and a straight body. Pull the chest to the rings, then lower.} TRX_ROW{Lean back holding the handles, body straight. Pull the chest to the handles, squeezing the shoulder blades, then lower.} TRX_Y_RAISE{Lean back holding the handles with straight arms. Raise the arms overhead into a Y shape, then return with control.} FACE_PULL_BAND{Anchor a band at face height. Pull the band toward the face with the elbows high and wide, then return slowly.} EXTERNAL_ROTATION_BAND{Elbow bent 90 degrees and tucked to the side. Rotate the forearm outward against the band, then return slowly.} DUMBBELL_ROW{Support one hand on a bench, back flat. Row the dumbbell to the hip and lower with control.} KETTLEBELL_SWING{Hinge at the hips and swing the bell back between the legs, then snap the hips forward to swing it to chest height.} DEADLIFT{Bar over mid-foot, hinge and grip. Push the floor away and stand tall with a flat back, then lower the bar along the legs.} ROMANIAN_DEADLIFT{Stand with dumbbells in front of the thighs. Hinge at the hips with a flat back until the hamstrings stretch, then stand up.} BODYWEIGHT_SQUAT{Feet shoulder width. Sit the hips down and back as deep as comfortable with heels down, then stand up.} GOBLET_SQUAT{Hold a kettlebell at the chest. Squat deep with an upright torso and elbows inside the knees, then stand.} SPLIT_SQUAT{Stand in a long stride. Lower the rear knee toward the floor, keeping the front shin near vertical, then push up.} BULGARIAN_SPLIT_SQUAT{Rear foot on a bench behind you. Lower straight down until the front thigh is parallel, then drive up.} REVERSE_LUNGE{Step one foot back and lower the rear knee toward the floor. Push through the front heel to return.} LATERAL_LUNGE{Step wide to one side and sit into that hip, keeping the other leg straight. Push back to standing.} STEP_UP{Place the whole foot on the box. Drive through the heel to stand up on it, then lower with control.} PISTOL_SQUAT_ASSISTED{Hold the straps for support. Squat down on one leg with the other extended forward, then stand up.} GLUTE_BRIDGE{Lie on the back with knees bent. Push through the heels to lift the hips until the body is straight, then lower.} SINGLE_LEG_GLUTE_BRIDGE{Lie on the back, one knee bent, the other leg extended. Lift the hips with the planted leg, then lower.} HIP_THRUST{Upper back on a bench, feet flat. Drive the hips up until the torso is level, squeeze, then lower.} NORDIC_CURL_ASSISTED{Kneel with the ankles held. Lower the body forward as slowly as possible, using the hands to catch and push back.} BACK_SQUAT{Bar on the upper back. Squat with the chest up and heels down as deep as comfortable, then drive up.} SINGLE_LEG_CALF_RAISE{Ball of one foot on the edge of a step. Rise as high as possible, pause, then lower the heel below the edge slowly.} PLANK{Forearms on the floor, body in one straight line. Brace the abs and glutes and hold without letting the hips sag.} SIDE_PLANK{Lie on one side on the forearm. Lift the hips so the body is straight and hold.} HOLLOW_HOLD{Lie on the back, press the lower back into the floor. Lift the shoulders and straight legs slightly and hold.} SUPERMAN_HOLD{Lie face down. Lift the arms, chest and legs off the floor and hold, looking down.} DEAD_BUG{Lie on the back with arms up and knees over the hips. Lower the opposite arm and leg toward the floor, keeping the lower back flat, and return.} BIRD_DOG{On hands and knees, extend the opposite arm and leg until level. Hold briefly, return, then switch.} HANGING_KNEE_RAISE{Hang from the bar. Lift the knees toward the chest with control and lower slowly without swinging.} HANGING_LEG_RAISE{Hang from the bar. Lift straight legs to horizontal or higher, then lower slowly without swinging.} L_SIT{Support on the hands with straight arms. Lift the straight legs to horizontal and hold.} MOUNTAIN_CLIMBER{From a plank, drive the knees alternately toward the chest at a steady pace, hips level.} RING_FALLOUT{Kneel holding the rings in front. Let the arms roll forward, extending the body, then pull back with the abs.} TRX_PIKE{Feet in the straps, hands on the floor in a plank. Lift the hips up into a pike, then return.} HANGBOARD_MAX_HANG{Hang from a comfortable edge with straight or slightly bent arms and active shoulders. Hold at high effort, then rest fully.} HANGBOARD_REPEATER{Hang on the edge for 7 seconds, rest 3 seconds, repeat for the set. Keep the shoulders active.} HANGBOARD_MIN_EDGE_HANG{Hang from the smallest edge you can hold with good form. Straight arms, active shoulders.} LOCK_OFF_HOLD{Pull up and hold with the elbow at about 90 degrees on one arm, using the other only as needed. Hold still.} TUCK_FRONT_LEVER{Hang, then pull the hips up with knees tucked until the back is horizontal. Straight arms, hold.} RICE_BUCKET{Push the hands into a bucket of rice and open, close, rotate and spread the fingers against the resistance.} WRIST_CURL{Forearms on the thighs, palms up. Curl the wrists up, then lower slowly.} REVERSE_WRIST_CURL{Forearms on the thighs, palms down. Lift the backs of the hands, then lower slowly.} BOULDER_PROBLEMS{Climb boulder problems at the given intensity with full rest between attempts. Focus on precise feet and controlled movement.} ROUTE_CLIMBING{Climb routes at the given intensity, resting fully between climbs. Keep the breathing steady.} ARC_TRAVERSE{Climb continuously on easy terrain at a low, sustainable pump for the whole time. Relax the grip.} LIMIT_BOULDERING{Work problems near your maximum with long rests. Few high-quality attempts, stop when form breaks.} FOUR_BY_FOUR{Climb four problems back to back, rest, and repeat four rounds. Choose problems well below your maximum.} EASY_RUN{Run at a relaxed pace where you could hold a conversation. Keep the effort easy throughout.} TEMPO_RUN{Run at a comfortably hard, steady pace you could sustain for about an hour.} INTERVAL_RUN{Alternate hard efforts with easy jogging recoveries. Keep the hard parts even in pace.} EASY_RIDE{Ride at an easy, conversational pace on flat terrain or low resistance.} STATIONARY_BIKE_STEADY{Pedal at a steady, moderate resistance and cadence for the whole time.} ROWING_ERG{Row with legs, then body, then arms; return arms, body, legs. Keep a steady, moderate stroke rate.} BURPEE{From standing, drop to a plank, do a push-up, jump the feet back in and jump up with arms overhead.} FOAM_ROLL_QUADS{Lie face down with the roller under the thighs. Roll slowly from hip to above the knee, pausing on tight spots.} FOAM_ROLL_UPPER_BACK{Roller under the upper back, hands behind the head. Roll slowly between the shoulder blades and mid-back.} FOAM_ROLL_CALVES{Roller under the calves, hands behind. Roll slowly from ankle to knee, turning the leg in and out.} FOREARM_MASSAGE{Use the thumb or a ball to press slowly along the forearm muscles, pausing on tender spots.} BOX_BREATHING{Breathe in for 4 seconds, hold 4, out for 4, hold 4. Repeat calmly.} WALKING_COOLDOWN{Walk at an easy pace, letting the breathing and heart rate settle.} other{{code}}}",
  "@exerciseInstructions": {"description": "How to perform the catalog exercise: start position, movement, return (C51 §8).", "placeholders": {"code": {"type": "String"}}},
  "exerciseCue": "{code, select, JUMPING_JACKS{Land softly, keep the knees soft.} HIGH_KNEES{Stay tall, do not lean back.} BUTT_KICKS{Keep the knees pointing down.} JUMP_ROPE{Small hops, wrists do the work.} ARM_CIRCLES{Keep the neck relaxed.} SHOULDER_DISLOCATES{Widen the grip if it pinches; never force it.} BAND_PULL_APART{Shoulders down, do not shrug.} HIP_CIRCLES{Keep the torso still, move only the hip.} LEG_SWINGS_FRONT{Controlled swings, do not bounce.} LEG_SWINGS_SIDE{Keep the hips facing the wall.} WRIST_CIRCLES{Slow and full range.} FINGER_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Mild stretch only, no pain.} FINGER_EXTENSOR_BAND{Slow on the way back.} SCAPULAR_PULL_UP{Elbows stay straight the whole time.} DEAD_HANG{Shoulders active, not hanging in the joints.} INCHWORM{Keep the legs as straight as comfortable.} EASY_TRAVERSE{Quiet feet, relaxed grip.} CAT_COW{Move with the breath, one vertebra at a time.} THORACIC_ROTATION{Rotate from the upper back, not the lower back.} WORLDS_GREATEST_STRETCH{Keep the front heel down.} DEEP_SQUAT_HOLD{Heels down; hold something if needed.} HIP_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Tuck the pelvis first, then shift forward.} PIGEON_STRETCH{Keep the hips square, no knee pain.} HAMSTRING_STRETCH{Flat back, hinge from the hips.} COUCH_STRETCH{Squeeze the glute, keep the torso upright.} CHILD_POSE{Breathe into the back and ribs.} DOWNWARD_DOG{Long spine, bend the knees if needed.} COBRA{Hips stay on the floor.} ANKLE_CIRCLES{Full slow circles.} CALF_RAISE{Full range, pause at the top.} SINGLE_LEG_BALANCE{Toes relaxed, arch lifted.} SHORT_FOOT{Do not curl the toes.} TOWEL_SCRUNCH{Slow, deliberate movement.} WRIST_FLEXOR_STRETCH{Elbow straight, gentle pull.} SHOULDER_CARS{Slow, torso still.} HIP_CARS{Torso still, move only the hip.} PUSH_UP{Body in one line; do not let the hips sag.} INCLINE_PUSH_UP{Elbows about 45 degrees from the body.} DIAMOND_PUSH_UP{Elbows close to the body.} PIKE_PUSH_UP{Head moves toward the floor, not forward.} RING_PUSH_UP{Keep the rings still; slow tempo.} RING_DIP{Turn the rings out at the top; skip if the shoulders hurt.} RING_SUPPORT_HOLD{Shoulders down and away from the ears.} TRX_CHEST_PRESS{Body straight, core braced.} TRX_TRICEPS_EXTENSION{Elbows point forward, upper arms still.} DUMBBELL_BENCH_PRESS{Shoulder blades down and back.} OVERHEAD_PRESS{Ribs down, do not arch the back.} BENCH_PRESS{Feet flat, controlled descent.} PULL_UP{Full range, no kipping.} CHIN_UP{Lower all the way each rep.} NEGATIVE_PULL_UP{Aim for 3-5 seconds down.} RING_ROW{Body straight like a plank.} TRX_ROW{Squeeze the shoulder blades at the top.} TRX_Y_RAISE{Straight arms, thumbs up.} FACE_PULL_BAND{Elbows high, hands to the ears.} EXTERNAL_ROTATION_BAND{Elbow stays tucked to the side.} DUMBBELL_ROW{Do not rotate the torso.} KETTLEBELL_SWING{Hips do the work, arms stay relaxed.} DEADLIFT{Flat back, bar close to the body.} ROMANIAN_DEADLIFT{Soft knees, hips back.} BODYWEIGHT_SQUAT{Knees track over the toes.} GOBLET_SQUAT{Chest up, elbows inside the knees.} SPLIT_SQUAT{Front shin near vertical.} BULGARIAN_SPLIT_SQUAT{Torso upright, front heel down.} REVERSE_LUNGE{Push through the front heel.} LATERAL_LUNGE{Keep both feet pointing forward.} STEP_UP{Do not push off the back foot.} PISTOL_SQUAT_ASSISTED{Use the straps as little as possible.} GLUTE_BRIDGE{Squeeze the glutes at the top.} SINGLE_LEG_GLUTE_BRIDGE{Hips level, do not twist.} HIP_THRUST{Chin tucked, ribs down.} NORDIC_CURL_ASSISTED{Straight line from knees to head.} BACK_SQUAT{Brace and keep the chest up.} SINGLE_LEG_CALF_RAISE{Slow lowering, full range.} PLANK{Squeeze glutes and abs; do not hold the breath.} SIDE_PLANK{Hips stacked, do not sag.} HOLLOW_HOLD{Lower back pressed to the floor.} SUPERMAN_HOLD{Look down to keep the neck neutral.} DEAD_BUG{Lower back stays flat.} BIRD_DOG{Hips level, do not rotate.} HANGING_KNEE_RAISE{No swinging; control the lowering.} HANGING_LEG_RAISE{Lower slowly, avoid swinging.} L_SIT{Push the floor away, shoulders down.} MOUNTAIN_CLIMBER{Hips level, no bouncing.} RING_FALLOUT{Do not let the lower back arch.} TRX_PIKE{Keep the legs straight.} HANGBOARD_MAX_HANG{Stop immediately on any sharp finger pain.} HANGBOARD_REPEATER{Consistent grip, no swinging.} HANGBOARD_MIN_EDGE_HANG{Never train fingers when they hurt.} LOCK_OFF_HOLD{Shoulder down, do not shrug.} TUCK_FRONT_LEVER{Straight arms, back flat.} RICE_BUCKET{Move slowly, all directions.} WRIST_CURL{Light weight, slow tempo.} REVERSE_WRIST_CURL{Small movement, no jerking.} BOULDER_PROBLEMS{Rest fully; quality over quantity.} ROUTE_CLIMBING{Breathe steadily, rest fully.} ARC_TRAVERSE{Low pump; slow down if the forearms burn.} LIMIT_BOULDERING{Stop when the form breaks.} FOUR_BY_FOUR{Keep it moving, easy problems.} EASY_RUN{You should be able to talk.} TEMPO_RUN{Steady, comfortably hard.} INTERVAL_RUN{Even pace on the hard parts.} EASY_RIDE{Easy pace, high cadence.} STATIONARY_BIKE_STEADY{Steady effort throughout.} ROWING_ERG{Legs first, arms last.} BURPEE{Land softly, keep the back flat.} FOAM_ROLL_QUADS{Slow, pause on tight spots.} FOAM_ROLL_UPPER_BACK{Do not roll the lower back.} FOAM_ROLL_CALVES{Slow, turn the leg in and out.} FOREARM_MASSAGE{Gentle pressure, breathe.} BOX_BREATHING{Slow and calm.} WALKING_COOLDOWN{Relax the shoulders.} other{}}",
